From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UniFrog Recovery <recovery@unifrog.local>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] freertos: disable HC16xx idle wait on SF2000

UniFrog retained crashes have shown reserved-instruction exceptions from
the FreeRTOS idle task while returning through the vendor display driver.
The idle hook was entering the HC16xx low-power wait instruction after
running registered callbacks. On SF2000/GB300 this path is not required
for correctness and can fault while the UI/report paths are otherwise idle.

Keep the idle hook as a callback runner and let the normal scheduler tick
wake the system.
---
 kernel/source/freertos/portable/GCC/MIPS32_HC16xx/port.c | 12 +++---------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/source/freertos/portable/GCC/MIPS32_HC16xx/port.c b/kernel/source/freertos/portable/GCC/MIPS32_HC16xx/port.c
index 0000000..0000000 100755
--- a/kernel/source/freertos/portable/GCC/MIPS32_HC16xx/port.c
+++ b/kernel/source/freertos/portable/GCC/MIPS32_HC16xx/port.c
@@ -241,16 +241,12 @@ void vApplicationIdleHook( void )
 		}
 	};
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_SOC_HC16XX
+	/*
+	 * SF2000/GB300 does not need the HC16xx low-power wait path here; kept
+	 * enabled it can raise EXC_RI from prvIdleTask after display/UI work.
+	 */
+	return;
 
-	if (get_processor_id() == 0)
-		return;
-
-	 __asm__("	.set	push		\n"
-		 "	.set	arch=r4000	\n"
-		 "	wait			\n"
-		 "	.set	pop 	\n");
-#endif
 }
 
 BaseType_t xPortIsInISR(void)
